st in unshown, so potentially dangerous (e.g., someone could be waiting on T7-T8-T9). But T8\u00d72 in hand suggests keeping one may support future chow, though unlikely.\n- Play T5: Middle tile, part of possible straight. But isolated.\n- Play J2: As established, **all four J2 tiles are accounted for** (3 in Peng by previous player, 1 in my hand), so **no one can use it**. This is a **safe discard**.\n\nReason: Discarding J2 is completely safe because all four copies are already visible (3 exposed in previous player\u2019s pung, 1 in my hand). No other player can use it. In contrast, discarding F2 (my seat wind), T8, or any dragon like J1/J3 risks helping opponents. F1 is safer than F2 but still less safe than J2. Therefore, **Play J2** is the optimal move.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
